# ============================================================================
# Whitelist build context for the `cc-lb` server image.
#
# Strategy: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include only the inputs the build
# actually consumes. This keeps the context small and deterministic — new files
# are excluded by default, so nothing leaks in accidentally.
#
# If you add a new *compile-time* input (an embedded asset, a codegen source,
# a new manifest), add a matching `!` rule below and re-verify with a real
# `docker buildx build`.
# ============================================================================

# 1) Ignore everything, recursively.
**

# 2) Cargo workspace graph: every member manifest + the lockfile are required to
#    resolve the workspace even for `cargo build -p cc-lb-server`.
!**/Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock

# 3) Rust sources and build scripts for every workspace member.
!**/*.rs

# 4) Toolchain pin + cargo configuration (musl target, linker, rustflags).
!rust-toolchain.toml
!.cargo/config.toml

# 5) Compile-time-embedded SQL migrations. The sqlite/postgres storage adapters
#    embed their `migrations/` dir via `sqlx::migrate!()`, and cc-lb-scheduler
#    `include_str!()`s its migration SQL. `sqlx::migrate!` reads the whole
#    directory at compile time, so whitelist all `.sql` rather than guessing.
!**/*.sql

# 6) cc-lb-admin dashboard SPA sources. `crates/cc-lb-admin/build.rs` builds and
#    embeds `web/dist` via Bun at compile time, so the web sources must be
#    present. Its own `node_modules` / build output are (re)generated in-image.
!crates/cc-lb-admin/web/**

# 7) The shared compile script the `compiled` stage runs (also used by the
#    docker-build CI `docker run`).
!scripts/build-cc-lb.sh

# 8) Re-exclude heavy or generated trees that the broad negations above would
#    otherwise pull back in. `.dockerignore` does NOT consult `.gitignore`, so a
#    local `target/` or `node_modules/` on disk must be excluded explicitly, and
#    these rules come last so they win.
**/target/**
**/node_modules/**
crates/cc-lb-admin/web/dist/**
crates/cc-lb-admin/web/dist-ssr/**
crates/cc-lb-admin/web/.vite/**
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The fuzz tree is a separate workspace, not built by `-p cc-lb-server`.
fuzz/**
